== 6. Gap Analysis: Tradition vs Modern Interpretation
<gap-analysis-tradition-vs-modern-interpretation>
=== 6.1 Where the tradition is correct
<where-the-tradition-is-correct>
- #strong[Copper has antimicrobial properties] — fully validated; copper
  surfaces actively kill bacteria and viruses
- #strong[Copper water vessels for storage are bioactively beneficial] —
  fully validated; ~3000-year-old practice anticipates modern science
- #strong[Tamra-bhasma is therapeutically active for liver and digestive
  disorders] — supported by modern research
- #strong[Specific copper-tin compositions produce different alloys with
  different properties] — fully validated; bell-bronze (22-24% tin) and
  mirror-bronze (32.6% tin) have distinct phase chemistry
- #strong[Copper as Mangala (Mars-quality fire/blood metal)] —
  internally coherent with copper’s high reactivity and red color
- #strong[The shodhana sequence converts copper toward oxide form] —
  accurately observed; modern XRD confirms phase progression
- #strong[Multiple putas required for complete conversion] — accurately
  observed; modern XRD shows 16-22 cycles needed
- #strong[Aranmula and bell-bronze tradition produces
  specifically-engineered intermetallics] — confirmed; preserved
  tradition with modern materials-science validation

=== 6.2 Where the tradition’s claims need qualification
<where-the-traditions-claims-need-qualification>
- #strong[Copper-Venus (Western convention)] — classical Indian
  copper-Mangala is the version this volume uses; cross-tradition
  disambiguation needed
- #strong[Specific clinical efficacy claims beyond ulcer/liver
  protection] — many secondary indications need rigorous study
- #strong[Some classical preparations using mercury-mediated route] —
  need to be distinguished from modern mercury-free protocols; the
  chemistry is different
- #strong["All copper preparations are interchangeable"] — they are not;
  tamra-bhasma (CuO), tamra-sindura (mercury-containing), and bronze
  alloys are chemically distinct preparations with different therapeutic
  profiles

=== 6.3 Where the framework can help
<where-the-framework-can-help>
- #strong[Copper operations have favorable timing across many
  nakshatras] — single Budha-enmity creates only narrow avoid-window
- #strong[Copper-tin alloy operations (Aranmula, bell-bronze) have
