== 10. Closing Notes
<closing-notes>
Copper has the broadest empirical-convergence record of any dhatu in the
compendium. Tamra-bhasma chemistry is fully characterized by modern XRD
as CuO nano-particles. Antimicrobial copper vessel use anticipates
modern public-health science. Aranmula delta bronze and bell-bronze beta
phase represent some of the world’s most precisely-engineered
intermetallic phase metallurgy — practiced empirically for millennia in
living traditions.

The framework predictions for copper operations are favorable across
many nakshatras due to Mangala’s friendships with Surya, Chandra, and
Guru. The single Budha-enmity creates narrow constraints that affect
mainly mercury-mediated copper preparations, where the
Pushya-as-stable-anchor pattern emerges consistently with other
multi-graha mercurial operations.

The Aranmula kannadi case represents the cleanest direct-validation
opportunity in the entire compendium. Bell-bronze acoustic analysis
represents the cheapest empirically-accessible validation pathway.
Either or both could be pursued with modest resources to test framework
predictions against a living tradition (Aranmula) or a
widespread-and-measurable practice (bell-bronze).

Copper’s cross-tradition correspondence (Mangala in Indian, Venus in
Western) is the second of two significant Indian-Western divergences in
the compendium (alongside iron-Shani/iron-Mars from Volume IV). Together
these establish that the classical Indian metallurgical-astrological
correspondence system has internal coherence distinct from Western
Hermetic alchemy — and may track physical properties more directly
through these specific assignments.

